jzmmc: ignore error interrupts that arrive with no request in flight

The tasklet forced STATE_ERROR on every error interrupt, including one that
arrives after the request has completed. The state machine then called
mmc_request_done() a second time on a stale host->mrq, whose cmd pointer is
no longer valid, and the kernel panicked in interrupt context.

Applies on top of 0099-jzmmc-drop-cmd53-crc-retry.patch.

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/jzmmc_v12.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/jzmmc_v12.c
@@ -543,6 +543,17 @@
 		clear_msc_irq(host, mask);
 		disable_msc_irq(host, mask);
 
+		/*
+		 * A late error interrupt can arrive after the request has
+		 * already been completed. host->mrq is stale by then, so
+		 * completing it again dereferences freed stack memory.
+		 */
+		if (host->state == STATE_IDLE) {
+			dev_warn(host->dev, "stale error irq ignored, iflg=0x%08X status=0x%08X\n",
+				 iflg, status);
+			goto out;
+		}
+
 		host->state = STATE_ERROR;
 		jzmmc_state_machine(host, status);
 		goto out;
